    "description": "Chapel, level 3 of 3: L2 plus flourish 3. Needs scaffolding: 13 tall (the bell cote; the nave roof is 9). Over budget: 600 blocks vs 210 (first build 371 vs 170; the L2 sacristy is about 90 and the L3 churchyard front 94; 7 wide instead of 5, for two pews a side). Stone chapel (stone bricks on a cobblestone plinth, buttresses, spruce gable roof) whose front gable rises into a bell cote; door under a stone hood, lancet windows, shuttered gable windows, pews, an altar; L2 adds the sacristy wing at the back, the bell, runner, lectern, candles, lanterns, flower boxes; L3 the churchyard front (a low churchyard wall with a lych gate, old headstones, a stone path, lantern posts), stained glass in the gable windows, banners, candles and flowers. Not yet builder-tested: azure_bluet, bell, blue_stained_glass_pane, candle, cornflower, dandelion, fern, lectern, lily_of_the_valley, mossy_cobblestone_slab, mossy_stone_brick_stairs, oxeye_daisy, red_stained_glass_pane, red_wall_banner, white_wall_banner, yellow_stained_glass_pane. Decoration step adds: banner_pattern, item, potted_plant.",
    "changes": "L2 now adds a feature seen from afar: the sacristy, a small stone wing at the back right with its own spruce gable roof, door, window and vestments chest (Carlton: not much differentiating L2 and L3). L3 keeps the walled churchyard front with the lych gate. The box grew 4 rows at the back.",
    "parent": 2,
